        "original_id": "320181c9-4a4d-5cff-ba1c-7fae2917af38",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mike Connors, Leon Danielian, Alec Guinness, Robert Redford, Joe Mannix\n- Works: Mannix, Situation Hopeless... But Not Serious\n- Awards: Golden Globe Awards, Emmy Awards\n- Roles: actor, private detective, ballet dancer, teacher, choreographer, educator\n\nFacts:\n- Leon Danielian was an American ballet dancer, teacher, choreographer, and educator who lived from 31 October 1920 to 8 March 1997.\n- Mike Connors, born Krekor Ohanian, was an Armenian-American actor who lived from August 15, 1925 to January 26, 2017.\n- Situation Hopeless... But Not Serious is a 1965 comedy film starring Alec Guinness, Mike Connors, and Robert Redford.\n- Mike Connors played private detective Joe Mannix in the CBS television series Mannix from 1967 to 1975.\n- Mike Connors won a Golden Globe Award in 1970 for Mannix, the first of six straight Golden Globe nominations.\n- Mike Connors received four consecutive Emmy nominations from 1970 through 1973 for Mannix.",
